{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"splurgy-tangible-halicore","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# No loop breaker: `tool_step_limit` is never set on the primary completion-verify step\n\nDiscovered while root-causing [rebar:bf31-fd55-d28d-4b7a]. An instrumented completion-verifier run\nagainst epic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb] (264 tool calls, 1074s) entered a closed 4-call cycle at\ncall #121 and repeated it 31-37x until the step budget killed the run. Calls 199-264 introduced\n**0% novel** tool-call signatures.\n\nNothing in the agent loop can detect or stop that. There is no tool-call dedup, and the shipped\nforced-landing primitive `RunRequest.tool_step_limit` — withdraw tools after N run steps, so the\nagent must conclude with what it has (`src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py:64-75`) — is **never set for the\nprimary verify step**: `build_agent_request` does not set it\n(`src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py:327-338`) and the gate YAML has no way to. Its only caller is the\nbounded recovery path (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:471`, `_EVIDENCE_TOOL_STEPS=16`).\n\nConsequence: a looping verifier is killed with NO verdict instead of being made to land with one.\n`docs/llm-framework.md:698-704` already states the project's position — \"a high recursion limit\nmeans *you're paying for a loop, fix the loop*\".\n\nbf31 removes ONE loop's fuel (a `search_files` false negative). This ticket is the structural guard\nthat makes any future loop survivable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the primary completion-verify agent step runs with a `tool_step_limit`, so tools are withdrawn\n      before the step budget is exhausted and the agent is forced to emit a verdict\n- [ ] a run that would previously have died budget-exhausted instead returns a completion_verdict\n      (a test drives a looping tool and asserts a verdict is produced, not an exception)\n- [ ] the limit is derived from the step budget rather than a second unrelated magic number\n- [ ] no change to a run that converges normally — an existing passing verification is unaffected","id":"c827-2a23-cd00-473e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion verifier has no loop breaker: tool_step_limit is never set on the primary verify step"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785932587884608001,"uuid":"f9719d7b-fa78-4ea2-bc8b-271312d5d309"}